But we also need to simulate getSchemaNode returns null. That depends on the JsonSchema instance. In test we would need to mock or subclass JsonSchema to override getSchemaNode to return null. For test case description we just note that schema node is null.

Thus test case format: input param propertyOrIndex, expected exception (NullPointerException), description.

For Number with faulty intValue: propertyOrIndex is instance of custom Number that overrides intValue to throw IllegalArgumentException. Expected IllegalArgumentException.

For Object with faulty toString: propertyOrIndex is custom object whose toString throws IllegalStateException. Expected IllegalStateException.

Thus produce JSON.

